  "Number": 2,
  "Question": "A refrigerator is offered for sale at \\(\\$250.00\\) less successive discounts of \\(20\\%\\) and \\(15\\%.\\) The sale price of the refrigerator is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(35\\%\\) less than \\(\\$250.00\\)",
    "B": "\\(65\\%\\) of \\(\\$250.00\\)",
    "C": "\\(77\\%\\) of \\(\\$250.00\\)",
    "D": "\\(68\\%\\) of \\(\\$250.00\\)",
    "E": "none of these"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The second discount applies to the price remaining after the first discount. A \\(20\\%\\) discount leaves \\(80\\%\\) of the price, and the following \\(15\\%\\) discount leaves \\(85\\%\\) of that reduced price. Thus the retained fraction of the original price is\n\\[\n0.80\\cdot0.85=0.68.\n\\]\nThe sale price is \\(68\\%\\) of \\(\\$250\\), namely \\(250\\cdot0.68=\\$170\\), choice D.",
